artifacts. Keep local execution and hosted CI execution distinct in your report: a

6
00:00:27,312 --> 00:00:31,725
working command on your workstation is preparation evidence, not proof that a remote

7
00:00:31,738 --> 00:00:33,338
pipeline ran successfully.

8
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:40,075
The laboratory includes an explicit defect switch that allows a repeated request to

9
00:00:40,088 --> 00:00:45,225
create another transfer. Run that variant on separate ports so the healthy classroom

10
00:00:45,238 --> 00:00:51,500
remains available. Use a dedicated terminal inside the distributed project. Set the

11
00:00:51,512 --> 00:00:55,812
synthetic hook value as documented, then start the variant with its gateway and

12
00:00:55,825 --> 00:01:01,912
service ports. This is a controlled experiment. Keep the environment address visible

13
00:01:01,925 --> 00:01:06,312
throughout the run so an expected failure from the defective version is never confused

14
00:01:06,325 --> 00:01:08,062
