32
00:02:33,512 --> 00:02:38,937
If they match, compare the returned identifiers and statuses. The defective teaching

33
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:44,100
variant can still return a replay-like status while creating another record. That is

34
00:02:44,112 --> 00:02:49,250
why status checks alone are insufficient. Follow the evidence into the account balance

35
00:02:49,262 --> 00:02:52,937
and transfer collection rather than stopping at HTTP metadata.

36
00:02:55,166 --> 00:03:00,678
The correct postcondition is ninety thousand centavos and one transfer. A duplicate

37
00:03:00,691 --> 00:03:05,016
debit would instead leave eighty thousand centavos and two records for this isolated

38
00:03:05,028 --> 00:03:11,841
opening state. Treat those actual values, when observed, as defect evidence. Do not

39
00:03:11,854 --> 00:03:17,128
change the expected balance, remove the count assertion, or add a skip. A good

40
00:03:17,141 --> 00:03:21,828
AI-assisted diagnosis explains how the request path violated the original rule and

41
00:03:21,841 --> 00:03:26,653
proposes an implementation correction. The regression remains the guardrail that

42
00:03:26,666 --> 00:03:29,841
distinguishes the corrected behavior from the teaching defect.

43
00:03:32,056 --> 00:03:36,844
Provide AI with the contract, relevant request excerpts, assertion message, and

44
00:03:36,856 --> 00:03:43,106
